/**
 * @file syscalls-doc.dox
 * @brief Linux syscall compatibility mapping for the FrostWing kernel.
 * @details
 * This document lists the syscall wrappers that are dispatched in
 * `syscalls/` and the internal kernel entry points they use.
 *
 * ## Core mapping
 * - `read(2)`              -> `sys_read()`              -> `vfs_read()` / `tty_read()`
 * - `write(2)`             -> `sys_write()`             -> `vfs_write()` / `putc()`
 * - `pipe(2)`              -> `fd_pipe_create()`        -> bounded in-kernel byte stream
 * - `open(2)` / `openat(2)`-> `sys_open_common()`       -> `fd_open()`
 * - `close(2)`             -> `sys_close()`             -> `fd_close()`
 * - `unlinkat(2)`          -> `sys_unlinkat()`          -> file unlink or empty-directory removal
 * - `lseek(2)`             -> `sys_lseek()`             -> fd position pointer update
 * - `getdents64(2)`        -> `sys_getdents64()`        -> FAT16/FAT32/ISO9660/proc/dev walkers
 * - `rename(2)`            -> `sys_rename()`            -> same-mount VFS rename
 * - `copy_file_range(2)`   -> `sys_copy_file_range()`   -> bounded VFS read/write loop
 * - `ftruncate(2)`         -> `sys_ftruncate()`         -> EXT2/FAT-backed file resizing
 * - `mount(2)`             -> `sys_mount()`             -> existing VFS mount backends
 * - `umount2(2)`           -> `sys_umount2()`           -> existing VFS unmount path
 *
 * ## File metadata
 * - `stat(2)`              -> `sys_stat()`              -> `fill_vfs_stat_for_path_at()`
 * - `fstat(2)`             -> `sys_fstat()`             -> `fill_vfs_stat_for_fd()`
 * - `newfstatat(2)`        -> `sys_newfstatat()`        -> `fill_vfs_stat_for_path_at()`
 * - `statx(2)`             -> `sys_statx()`             -> `sys_newfstatat()`
 * - `utimes(2)` / `futimesat(2)` / `utimensat(2)` -> FAT and EXT2 timestamp updates
 *
 * ## Memory management
 * - `mmap(2)`              -> `sys_mmap()`              -> `userland_mmap_anon()`
 * - `mprotect(2)`          -> `sys_mprotect()`          -> validation + no-op (current VM model)
 * - `madvise(2)`           -> `sys_madvise()`           -> validates ranges and accepts basic access-pattern hints
 * - `munmap(2)`            -> `sys_munmap()`            -> validation + no-op (current VM model)
 * - `brk(2)`               -> `sys_brk()`               -> `userland_brk()`
 * - `eventfd2(2)`          -> `sys_eventfd2()`          -> shared counter descriptors with read/write/poll
 *
 * ## Process and thread compatibility
 * - `execve(2)`            -> `sys_execve()`            -> `userland_exec()` / `execute_chain()`
 * - `fork(2)` / `clone(2)` -> `sys_fork()`              -> `multitasking_spawn_userland()` (exec-context clone)
 * - `clone3(2)`            -> `sys_clone3()`            -> restricted fork-compatible clone arguments
 * - `setfsuid(2)` / `setfsgid(2)` -> accept changes while all processes use root credentials
 * - `wait4(2)`             -> `sys_wait4()`             -> multitasking task-state polling
 * - `set_tid_address(2)`   -> `sys_set_tid_address()`   -> kernel clear-child-tid bookkeeping
 * - `set_robust_list(2)`   -> `sys_set_robust_list()`   -> ABI validation
 * - `tgkill(2)`            -> `sys_tgkill()`            -> argument validation + stubbed signal path
 *
 * ## Socket compatibility
 * - `socket(2)`            -> `sys_socket()`            -> IPv4 ICMP, UDP, and TCP sockets
 * - `poll(2)`              -> `sys_poll()`              -> UDP/ICMP socket readiness and descriptor validation
 * - `connect(2)`           -> `sys_connect()`           -> UDP peer selection or TCP handshake
 * - `sendto(2)` / `recvfrom(2)` -> `sys_sendto()` / `sys_recvfrom()` -> ICMP, UDP, and TCP data paths
 * - `recvmsg(2)` / `getsockname(2)` -> socket receive (including `IP_RECVTTL`) and local-address queries
 * - `SIOCGIF*` ioctls       -> basic `lo` and `eth0` interface information
 * - socket `read(2)` / `write(2)` -> socket receive/send paths
 *
 * ## Time and randomness
 * - `gettimeofday(2)`     -> `sys_gettimeofday()`   -> RTC-backed seconds and zeroed timezone
 * - `clock_gettime(2)`     -> `sys_clock_gettime()`  -> RTC-backed time fetch
 * - `nanosleep(2)`         -> `sys_nanosleep()`      -> `sleep()`
 * - `pselect6(2)`          -> `sys_pselect6()`       -> descriptor readiness via `sys_poll()`
 * - `getrandom(2)`         -> `sys_getrandom()`         -> xorshift seeded from `rdtsc64()`
 * - `ioctl(BLKGETSIZE64)`   -> block-device byte capacity from devfs
 * - `ioctl(RTC_RD_TIME)`    -> CMOS RTC time from `/dev/rtc0`
 * - terminal ioctls        -> accepted only for the kernel shell's tty descriptors and `/dev/tty`
 *
 * ## Procfs compatibility
 * - `/proc/filesystems` lists the filesystem implementations supported by VFS
 * - `/proc/modules` is empty because drivers are built into the kernel
 * - `/proc/net/dev` provides the Linux interface/counter table for `lo` and `eth0`
 */
